nize  from the Transformers and Resident Evil  series we'll have to wait until August  10th 2018 to get a look at Meg but that  look will be in 3d IMAX and will involve  Jason Statham fighting a giant shark so  of course it'll be worth the wait  cadaver Shay Mitchell makes the jump  from TVs Pretty Little Liars to  big-screen [ __ ]  with cadaver an intriguing project also  starring castles stana katic Mitchell  stars as a more technician and disgraced  former cop whose late night shifts take  a turn for the sinister and she receives  a badly brutalized corpse kind of like  this you'll see human heads without  bodies audiences will have to wait until  August 24th 2018 to get a look at  cadaver but director Dietrich van Rijn  is already on to his next project he's  tapped to handle an upcoming remake of  Alfred Hitchcock's classic The Byrds  Halloween reboots of classic horror  franchises haven't exactly been  cinematic gold in recent years with new  installments of Nightmare on Elm Street  and Friday the 13th leaving fans  wondering if these franchises were  better off dead since Rob Zombie remade  Halloween in 2007 and did a sequel to it  in 2009 we understand if you're not too  excited about a new Halloween but here's  the thing you should be for one key  reason this is my moment eastbound and  down star Danny McBride and producer  David Gordon Green came together to work  on the new film which will serve as a  sequel for the first two films I think  tension is what it's all about is  keeping that tension in keeping people's  stomach in knots Michael Myers will  return at theaters on October 19 2018  just in time for the scariest night of  the year  The Strangers - The Strangers was a  surprise hit in 2008 and that many fans  were expecting the second installment  which was announced way back in 2009 to  actually see the light of day but a  decade after the first film in theaters  it's coming with original director  johannes robert and writer bryan bertino  on board Christina Hendricks leads the  cast of the film which has an as-yet  undetermined release date into one  18 what we do know is that it reportedly  takes place at a trailer park in the  middle of nowhere  during a power outage where an  appearance by sac head and pin-up girl  would definitely be something to scream  about nas farhat to the witch is widely  considered to be among the scariest  films of 2015 a unique and ambitious  debut by director robert Eggers and for  his follow-up Eggers is not scaling back  on his ambition he'll be helming a  remake of the seminal 1922 horror  classic nods ferrata  an undertaking only attempted once  before in 1979 by acclaimed German  filmmaker Werner Herzog's Eggers is a  lifelong fan of the original film has  even mounted a stage production twice  it's safe to say that the remake is in  very good hands and if the witch is any  indication fans might be in for the  creepiest vampire flick in years  abruptio Buffy the Vampire Slayer's  James Marsters stars in this intriguing  film playing it down on his luck regular  Joe who wakes up one morning with a bomb  implanted in his neck and there's one  hell of a twist you can imagine but  they're all involved that's right all  the film's roles will be performed by  life-sized realistic latex puppets and  it's got a hell of a supporting cast  including comedian turned horror  mastermind Jordan Peele  of rusty Oh will hit theaters sometime  in 2018 and we can only hope we're ready  [Music]  Winchester  now this looks really cool Winchester is  inspired by the true and very bizarre  story of firearm heiress  Sarah Winchester whose mansion is the  stuff of legend a house crowded in  mystery and speculation a house that has  been the source of one of the most  unusual legends in California history  Winchester supposedly believed that the  ghosts of people killed by her family's  firearms would haunt her forever  unless she never stopped building  rotating ships of carpenters worked on  the mansion until Winchester's death in  1922  creating an endless series of rooms  nooks in the hallways little corridors  that maybe once went somewhere if it  wasn't a constant safety cover that the  unusual really never stops in this house  the upcoming film is a supernatural  period piece written and directed by  identical twins peter and michael  spierig who were behind the 2009 sci-fi  horror thriller day breakers but key to  this project is the casting of Helen  Mirren in the lead role  bringing the kind of acting chops that  can elevate any material Winchester is  slated for release on February 23rd 2018  thanks for watching click the looper  icon to subscribe to our YouTube channel  plus check out all this cool stuff we  know you'll love to  [Music]

